    "body": "Hmm, I'm unclear what you're expecting here. The spec is pretty clear in https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/input.html#the-step-attribute what happens when it's set to `any`; there is no allowed value step, and so constraint validation does not check that constraint.\r\n\r\nI can't find any other uses of the word \"any\" in any other input type specifications, so I don't understand \"Unlike for other types to which step applies\". No specific input types seem to mention `any`; it's all defined in that centralized section that I linked to.",
